    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n1253" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀδηνής</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ές</span>,
			(<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">δῆνος</span>) <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>ignorant, inexperienced</i>, <i><span class="en">
				Semon.
				7.53
			</span></i>, cj. for <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἁληνής</span>, but expl.
			as <i>'without malice prepense'</i> by Hsch, <i><span class="en">
				<u>EM</u>
				17.11
			</span></i>: so in Adv.
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">-έως</span>
			<i>without malice</i>, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">διὰ τῆς πόλεως ἀ. γεγωνέοντες</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					<u>GDI</u>
					5653
				</span></i>
			 (<span class="entity">Chios</span>):—hence <b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀδήλ-εια</span></b> , ἡ, <i>ignorance</i>, Hsch (<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">-είη</span>).</div>
